.\" dbsql(1) -- the dbsql command-line shell.
.TH DBSQL 1 "October 2026" "dbsql 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dbsql \- command-line interface to dbsql databases (SQLite SQL on Berkeley DB)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dbsql
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ filename
.RI [ SQL ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dbsql
is the interactive shell for dbsql, the SQL language of SQLite 3.53.4
running on Berkeley DB (libdb) storage.  It reads SQL statements and
dot-commands from the terminal or from standard input, runs them
against the database
.IR filename ,
and prints the results.  SQL given on the command line is run in order
and the shell exits.
.PP
If
.I filename
is omitted the database is a transient in-memory database
.RB ( :memory: ).
A file that does not exist is created.
.PP
A dbsql database is a single libdb file; its tables and indexes are
sub-databases of that file.  The directory holding the file is a libdb
environment: it also holds libdb's region files
.RB ( __db.* )
and transaction logs
.RB ( log.* ),
which together with the file are the database.  Copy a database with
.BR .backup ,
.B VACUUM INTO
or the online backup API, not by copying the file while it is in use.
Opening a database whose environment was not shut down cleanly runs
libdb recovery.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
$ dbsql ex1.db
dbsql version 1.1.0 (SQL 3.53.4, libdb storage)
Enter ".help" for usage hints.
dbsql> CREATE TABLE tbl1(one TEXT, two INTEGER);
dbsql> INSERT INTO tbl1 VALUES('hello!', 10), ('goodbye', 20);
dbsql> SELECT * FROM tbl1;
hello!|10
goodbye|20
dbsql> .quit
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat no subsequent arguments as options.
.TP
.B \-ascii, \-box, \-column, \-csv, \-html, \-json, \-line, \-list, \-markdown, \-quote, \-table, \-tabs
Set the output mode.
.TP
.B \-bail
Stop after the first error.
.TP
.B \-batch
Force batch I/O.
.TP
.BI \-cmd " command"
Run
.I command
before reading standard input.
.TP
.B \-echo
Print each input before running it.
.TP
.BI \-escape " T"
How control characters are shown: symbol, ascii or off.
.TP
.BR \-header ", " \-noheader
Turn column headers on or off.
.TP
.B \-help
Show the options.
.TP
.B \-ifexists
Open the database only if it already exists.
.TP
.BI \-init " file"
Read and process
.I file
(dot-commands and SQL) at startup.
.TP
.B \-interactive
Force interactive I/O.
.TP
.BI \-newline " sep"
Output row separator (default newline).
.TP
.B \-nofollow
Refuse to open a database through a symbolic link.
.TP
.B \-noinit
Do not read
.BR ~/.dbsqlrc .
.TP
.BI \-nullvalue " text"
Text shown for NULL (default empty).
.TP
.B \-readonly
Open the database read-only.
.TP
.B \-safe
Safe mode: refuse commands that touch files or run programs.
.TP
.BI \-separator " sep"
Output column separator (default |).
.TP
.B \-stats
Print memory statistics after each statement.
.TP
.B \-version
Show the dbsql, SQL and libdb versions.
.PP
The remaining options
.RB ( \-append ,
.BR \-lookaside ,
.BR \-mmap ,
.BR \-pagecache ,
.BR \-vfs ", ...)"
are accepted for compatibility with the SQLite shell; options that
configure SQLite's pager or file format have no effect on libdb storage.
.SH DOT-COMMANDS
Lines beginning with a period are commands to the shell.
.B .help
lists them all;
.B ".help \-all"
gives details.  Commonly used:
.TP
.B .tables ", " .schema " ?pattern?"
List tables, show CREATE statements.
.TP
.B .mode " mode" ", " .headers " on|off"
Output format.
.TP
.BI .import " file table"
Import CSV or other delimited data.
.TP
.B .dump " ?objects?"
Render the database as SQL.
.TP
.BI .backup " ?db? file" ", " .restore " ?db? file"
Online backup and restore.
.TP
.BI .open " file" ", " .databases
Open another database; list attached databases.
.TP
.BI .read " file" ", " .output " ?file?" ", " .once " file"
Read input from a file; send output to a file.
.TP
.B .timer " on|off" ", " .eqp " on|off|full"
Statement timing; automatic EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN.
.TP
.BI .timeout " ms"
Retry for up to
.I ms
milliseconds when the database is locked by another connection.
.TP
.B .quit
Exit.
.SH CONCURRENCY
Readers see a consistent snapshot and never block writers; one
connection writes a database at a time (another writer gets
.B "database is locked"
until it commits or the
.B .timeout
expires).  These are SQLite WAL-mode semantics, provided by libdb's
multi-version concurrency control.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.dbsqlrc
Read at startup unless
.B \-noinit
is given.
.TP
.I dir/__db.* , dir/log.*
The libdb environment of databases in directory
.IR dir .
.SH SEE ALSO
https://codeberg.org/gregburd/dbsql
